[{:db/id "q-107060/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "680995e6-a209-5e11-a827-cf8d8c1e6261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f0f1c010-5011-5481-80a3-0cb47f139182" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "da8005e6-e2e8-5d45-ba27-fd29abaeb9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b9a5187b-9604-5273-b91a-7be182b0cb4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ce55d0f9-0f9c-5ff3-bcb6-f447db927598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34a2c02c-86e3-5c46-9a01-8a0355ee52d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107060/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-107060/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-107060/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-107060/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-107060/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-107060/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107060" :question/id #uuid "e9530e94-2077-5cc5-bfa5-d3da05501ed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107060" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}-1}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2x-7}-1)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{2x-7})}^{2}-{1}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-7-1}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-8}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2(x-4)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107060/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338477/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f91dc651-1dcb-55c0-ad58-2fb6f060c3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338477/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1b842499-2b2e-53b1-82ab-9f617a433e0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338477/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2466bdcc-8923-54b6-89fe-6cd1638dce50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338477/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-338477/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-338477/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338477" :question/id #uuid "060847a0-f068-589c-94fd-9b85a0de164c" :question/math-academy-id "q-338477" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & =\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5(5)}}{5-5}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{(5-\\sqrt{5x})(5+\\sqrt{5x})}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{{5}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5x})}^{2}}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{25-5x}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5(5-x)}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5\\cancel{(5-x)}}{\\cancel{(5-x)}(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5(5)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338477/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338504/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "573c49ce-e5d8-54dd-897a-3b5674cac952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338504/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "99721541-de5a-5611-85b3-e921e432021d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338504/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-338504/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338504" :question/id #uuid "25bce61b-a5f1-5031-96bf-625853eef9f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-338504" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=3$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & =\\frac{3-3}{3(3)-\\sqrt{27(3)}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x-\\sqrt{27x})(3x+\\sqrt{27x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{27x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9{x}^{2}-27x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x(x-3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{27x}}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3)+\\sqrt{27(3)}}{9(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+9}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338504/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
